# Build context for the GAME SERVER image.
#
# server/Dockerfile builds from the repository root rather than from server/,
# because the server now depends on packages/engine and a context rooted at
# server/ cannot see a sibling directory. That makes everything in the repo
# part of the context, so the expensive and dangerous things are excluded here.
#
# `data/` matters most: it is the Postgres bind mount from docker-compose.yml.
# Sending it would be slow at best, and reading a running database's data
# directory fails on permissions at worst.
#
# api/ has its own context (./api) and its own api/.dockerignore; nothing here
# affects it.

# Dependencies and build output, at every level
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
server_dist

# The database bind mount and local backups
data
postgres_data

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.vscode

# Secrets — never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Client-only assets. The game server serves no static files, and these are the
# bulk of the repository.
public
src
index.html
*.log

# Docs, the documentation site, tooling and tests: not part of any runtime artifact
docs
website
scripts
artifacts
tests
*.md
